<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Transcaucasian Sejm</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Transcaucasian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sejm">Sejm</a> was the legislature of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-caucasus">Transcaucasia</a> that met in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tbilisi">Tiflis</a> from February to May 1918, formed from Georgian, Armenian and Azerbaijani deputies elected to the Russian Constituent Assembly. Under Ottoman military pressure after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-brest-litovsk">Treaty of Brest-Litovsk</a>, it declared the Transcaucasian Democratic Federative Republic independent on 22 April 1918. Divided by national rivalries, it dissolved on 26 May 1918, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> declared independence, followed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/transcaucasian-sejm.jpg" alt="Transcaucasian Sejm" width="320" height="216" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Russian Tzar Ministry of Internal Affairs · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map-1903-caucasus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
